      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "This is a really cool idea, I'd LOVE for it to be implemented. Additionally, making it a trigger, allows the community to create a super cool camera that has way more features than even the mod only camera, since we can attach arbitrary objects to a camera, including filters using custom shaders, etc.\n\nHowever this is also super dangerous if not implemented in a way that limits how often a picture can be taken, and offers a preview of the image for the user to first consent to, before it is saved onto their hard drive.\n\nThe reason for this is that otherwise a malicious user could make a room that on spawn, triggers a local only event that rapidly takes hi-res photos, filling up their hard drive instantly, or worse, automatically takes a bunch of photos of illegal images that are located in the room somewhere, filling everyone's hard drives with illegal images without them even knowing it.\n\nSo yeah, I love the idea, but we have to be super smart and cautious about implementation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-03-02T14:51:15.933Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This proposed (local only) trigger would connect to a reference camera in the world and save a screenshot of the camera view to the users VRC photo folder.  This would allow world creators to add \"photo spots\", photo booths or movable cameras in their worlds where users could take group photos.  The functionality is already there to add a visible countdown timer for everyone to get in position.",
